To prevent BGP route reflectors from reflecting routes back to members of the same neighbor group, use the `disable-client-reflect` command at the group level. This stops the route reflector from re-advertising routes learned from one client to other clients in the same group, while still allowing proper route distribution to external peers.

```cli
configure router bgp group "RR-CLIENTS"
    disable-client-reflect
exit
```

**Key points:**  
- Apply `disable-client-reflect` under the BGP group containing the route reflector clients.  
- Replace `"RR-CLIENTS"` with your actual group name.  
- Routes learned from external peers or other groups will still be advertised to clients.  

