To adjust the BGP Connect Retry interval to 90 seconds, use the following CLI command in the appropriate BGP configuration context:

```
configure router bgp
   connect-retry 90
exit
```

This command sets the timer to **90 seconds**, which controls how long the router waits before attempting to reconnect after a failed BGP session initiation. Apply it under:
- `config>router>bgp` (global BGP context)
- `config>router>bgp>group` (specific BGP group)
- `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor` (specific BGP neighbor)

The default value is **120 seconds**, so this change reduces the wait time.
