To ensure LLGR stale routes propagate consistently to all eBGP peers during graceful restart, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp graceful-restart long-lived
    advertised-stale-time 86400
    advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors without-no-export
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `advertised-stale-time 86400` sets the LLGR stale route retention period to 86400 seconds (24 hours), ensuring peers maintain routes during maintenance. Adjust the value as needed.  
- `advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors without-no-export` forces stale route advertisement to **all** eBGP peers (including those without LLGR capability) and removes the `no-export` barrier, allowing prefixes to exit your AS.  

Apply this globally under `bgp>graceful-restart>long-lived` to affect all address families and peers. For granular control, configure under specific `group`, `neighbor`, or `family` contexts.
