To implement BGP configuration for effectively combining and applying aggregated bandwidth metrics from EBGP neighbors on your Nokia 7750 SR routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group "EBGP_GROUP"
            link-bandwidth
                add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
                aggregate-used-paths ipv4
```

### Key Details:
1. **`link-bandwidth`**  
   Enters the configuration context for handling link-bandwidth extended communities.

2. **`add-to-received-ebgp ipv4`**  
   Automatically appends a link-bandwidth extended community to all received IPv4 routes from directly connected EBGP peers. This enables bandwidth tracking for incoming routes.

3. **`aggregate-used-paths ipv4`**  
   Aggregates bandwidth values from link-bandwidth communities of active multipaths when re-advertising routes with `next-hop-self`. This ensures consolidated bandwidth is applied for IPv4 routes.

### Notes:
- Replace `"EBGP_GROUP"` with your actual BGP group name.
- These commands assume EBGP peers are directly connected (single-hop), as required by `add-to-received-ebgp`.
- Both commands target IPv4 unlabeled unicast routes, aligning with your requirement for IPv4 routes from external autonomous systems.
