To implement BGP-based load balancing with accurate bandwidth aggregation during redistribution using next-hop-self, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp group "TO_JUNIPER" link-bandwidth
    add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
exit
```

```cli
configure router bgp group "INTERNAL" link-bandwidth
    aggregate-used-paths ipv4
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- The first block enables link-bandwidth handling for the EBGP group facing Juniper peers (`TO_JUNIPER`). The `add-to-received-ebgp ipv4` command attaches link-bandwidth extended communities to IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers, using the physical interface's bandwidth value.  
- The second block configures the internal BGP group (`INTERNAL`) to sum bandwidth attributes from multipaths. The `aggregate-used-paths ipv4` command aggregates bandwidth values from link-bandwidth communities of active ECMP paths when readvertising IPv4 routes with next-hop-self.  

This ensures locally readvertised prefixes maintain accurate aggregated bandwidth metrics for load balancing across parallel links.
