To ensure BGP sessions remain stable during temporary disruptions, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
    group "your-group-name" 
        neighbor <neighbor-IP>
            hold-time 300 min 300
            damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 5 15 60 error-interval 30
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `graceful-restart`: Enables BGP session preservation during control plane restarts.  
- `hold-time 300 min 300`: Sets a 300-second hold timer and requires peers to accept this minimum value.  
- `damp-peer-oscillations`: Configures backoff timers to delay session resets (`5 15 60` = initial/second/max wait in minutes) and requires 30 error-free minutes to reset penalties.  

**Notes:**  
1. Replace `"your-group-name"` and `<neighbor-IP>` with your actual BGP group and peer IP.  
2. Adjust hold-time values based on expected disruption duration.  
3. Ensure peers support matching `graceful-restart` capabilities.  

This combination prevents premature session teardowns by extending failure tolerance and suppressing rapid session resets.
