To enforce a local LLGR stale time of one hour (3600 seconds) and override any conflicting values advertised by peers, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 3600
        long-lived
            advertised-stale-time 3600
            helper-override-stale-time 3600
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `stale-routes-time 3600` sets the local maximum retention time for stale routes to one hour.  
- `advertised-stale-time 3600` advertises one hour as the desired LLGR stale time to peers.  
- `helper-override-stale-time 3600` forces peers to use your one-hour setting, ignoring their advertised values.  

This configuration applies globally to all BGP peers and ensures consistent LLGR behavior while maintaining routing stability.
