Based on your network redesign requirements to prioritize traffic through the primary transit provider and ensure persistent configuration, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    local-preference 200
```

This configuration sets the BGP local preference attribute to **200** for all inbound route advertisements at the global BGP level. The change will:
- Affect routes received from all BGP peers
- Persist across router reloads
- Maintain a clean hierarchical policy structure

For more granular control, you can apply the command at the group or neighbor level:
```
configure router bgp group "PRIMARY_TRANSIT"
    local-preference 200
```
or
```
configure router bgp group "PRIMARY_TRANSIT" neighbor "192.0.2.1"
    local-preference 200
```
Replace `PRIMARY_TRANSIT` and `192.0.2.1` with your actual group and neighbor identifiers.
