   Apply the families within a dedicated group (e.g., `DC_FABRIC`) to limit scope to data center fabric peers. Replace placeholders (`DC_FABRIC`, peer-AS, neighbor IPs) with actual values.

### Critical Considerations:
- **Global vs. Group-Level Family Configuration**:  
  The `family` command at the global level (`config>router>bgp`) enables capabilities for the entire BGP instance. Override or extend this at the group/neighbor level as needed.  
