      entry 10
         from as-path-group "FilterLocalAS"
         action reject
      exit
      entry 20
         action accept
      exit
   exit
   commit
exit
```

Apply the policy to relevant BGP neighbors or groups:
```cli
/configure router bgp
   group <peer-group-name>
      import "Drop-Local-AS-Paths"
   exit
exit
```

**Key notes:**
1. Replace `<local-as>` with your actual local AS number (e.g., `expression 1 "^65001 .*"`)
2. Replace `<peer-group-name>` with your BGP peer group name
3. The policy:
   - Rejects routes where your AS appears anywhere in the AS_PATH (entries 10-40)
   - Accepts all other routes (entry 50)
4. Session stability is maintained as routes are silently dropped instead of triggering session resets

For per-neighbor application instead of group-level:
```cli
/configure router bgp
   neighbor <ip-address>
      import "Drop-Local-AS-Paths"
   exit
exit
